From 4322c8304231bd3f933c2d29edbcd4eff2ec33f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(cli): report wait --for delete the same way whatever
 the timing

wait --for delete printed "deleted" when it had seen the service before
it disappeared and "not found" when its first read already got a 404.
After delete returns 202 the controller can finish removing the service
before that first read, so the same commands printed one or the other
depending on timing, and "not found" read like an error although both
cases exit 0. The e2e test, whose controller polls every 50 ms, failed
intermittently because of it (3 of 60 runs here).

What wait --for delete waits for is that the service does not exist, so
it now prints "<service> deleted" and exits 0 whether or not it saw the
service first, as kubectl wait --for=delete does for an object that is
already gone. The README and the --help exit code table state that a
404 means success for wait --for delete rather than exit code 3, and
the README notes that a wrong name or namespace is reported as success
too.
